{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/793498-vascu-and-x-files","id":793498,"title":"VASCU and X-Files","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-27T03:59:56-08:00","id":793498,"title":"VASCU and X-Files","content":"So waiting for the <a href=\"http://www.denofgeek.us/tv/the-x-files/243258/the-x-files-revival-news-everything-we-know\" target=\"_blank\">new season/reboot of <b>X-Files</b></a> in January of 2016, I rewatch original series. Of course I have very <b>Hunter</b> thoughts, mostly of coming 2ED corebook and reprint of VASCU FBI Conspiracy ( from <b>Slasher</b> book ). I compare them with X-Files FBI cell in TV series and they look like totally two different organisations. I initially wanted to have X-Files to be just name for VASCU agents on &quot;our jurisdiction ceses&quot;, but more I read about conspiracy, less it looks like true FBI. It also much more strongly in serial killers than in typical hunter cases...<br /> <br /> According to the 1ED write-up, VASCU is just a bunch of psychics that normally would not pass tests for field agents. But Mulder and Scully are really <i>true</i> FBI members, and concerned mostly with good field work and suspect profiling. So maybe the X-Files is <b>other </b>Hunter organisation in the FBI? The more like Compact, or even Cell in kind? Looks to read your thoughts on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T04:13:42-08:00","id":793500,"title":"","content":"Huh? It says that part of the VASCU member <i>are</i> trained FBI agents (that were transfered after they were found compatible with the Wintergreen Process). The untrained ones are new recruits taken in solely because they are compatible (they get the training later). And VASCU <i>does</i> profiling and field work - that what their Endowment is designed to help with. And, technically, Teleinformatics isn't psychic, but drug-enhanced information processing (that is pretty much identical to psychic powers, unfortunately).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T04:21:11-08:00","id":793505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/793498-vascu-and-x-files#post793498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So waiting for the <a href=\"http://www.denofgeek.us/tv/the-x-files/243258/the-x-files-revival-news-everything-we-know\" target=\"_blank\">new season/reboot of <b>X-Files</b></a> in January of 2016, I rewatch original series. Of course I have very <b>Hunter</b> thoughts, mostly of coming 2ED corebook and reprint of VASCU FBI Conspiracy ( from <b>Slasher</b> book ). I compare them with X-Files FBI cell in TV series and they look like totally two different organisations. I initially wanted to have X-Files to be just name for VASCU agents on &quot;our jurisdiction ceses&quot;, but more I read about conspiracy, less it looks like true FBI. It also much more strongly in serial killers than in typical hunter cases...<br /> <br /> According to the 1ED write-up, VASCU is just a bunch of psychics that normally would not pass tests for field agents. But Mulder and Scully are really <i>true</i> FBI members, and concerned mostly with good field work and suspect profiling. So maybe the X-Files is <b>other </b>Hunter organisation in the FBI? The more like Compact, or even Cell in kind? Looks to read your thoughts on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a player bring up a similar question in our Hunter game. She liked the premise of VASCU, but didn't see her character having powers. After talking it over we just figured that her character didn't have to take the Endowment and that there were members of the Conspiracy that didn't take to the Process readily. I'm not sure if that is something you could see doing. If not you could just remove the Endowment and use the rest of the information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T04:38:37-08:00","id":793512,"title":"","content":"Thing with the X Files is that you've got all the tasty narrative scar tissue that sometimes intrudes back into the present from Mulder's time in Behavioural Science/Violent Crimes where he was fairly competant at catching (or helping to catch) killers. Thaty'd be an interesting way to play it; an agent drawn in to things they don't understand and then blindsided with post-Wintergreen truth. Having to adapt to a world they no longer recognise and cases that defy rationality.<br /> <br /> There's always headcanon ways to make it work; as above, why not just have non-Wintergreened agents who're there to provide more solid backbone to the unit or who've encountered Slashers etc, but don't have the 'gift'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T09:04:32-08:00","id":793604,"title":"","content":"Could Unseen Sense (Slashers) work as a replacement for Teleinformatics for a mundane VASCU member?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T09:25:13-08:00","id":793617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/793498-vascu-and-x-files?p=793604#post793604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could Unseen Sense (Slashers) work as a replacement for Teleinformatics for a mundane VASCU member?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see how that could work, but other Conspiracies have Unseen Sense as part of their status progression so I am not sure if that would be enough differentiation. What your post does make me think about is how it would be interesting from a developer perspective to work into the 2e a way of creating mundane members for Conspiracies that could possibly be brought into a 2nd tier chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T09:42:49-08:00","id":793638,"title":"","content":"Or that first Teleinformatics power, always, would be Unseen Sences (Slashers) - the next would be more typical supernatural in use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T09:54:07-08:00","id":793645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/793498-vascu-and-x-files?p=793638#post793638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or that first Teleinformatics power, always, would be Unseen Sences (Slashers) - the next would be more typical supernatural in use.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand that, but doesn't Unseen Sense kind of eliminate the whole having to find Slashers through investigation. I think one of the benefits of them as antagonists is that they are still functionally human (in most cases). If every member of VASCU got a tingle everytime they were around one wouldn't that defeat that part of their edge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T09:58:21-08:00","id":793647,"title":"","content":"I think Unseen Sense (Slashers), Status(FBI/VASCU), Contacts/Mentor/Ally (VASCU Hunters) and Professional Training (VASCU Agent, Investigation+Empathy) are all useful merits that non-endowed Hunters and non-Hunters could have as VASCU agents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T14:53:32-08:00","id":795104,"title":"","content":"As I made them for &quot;Think of fictional characters&quot; topic, I thought I share with you iconic pair of VASCU hunters. In this version they both run Tier 1 cell amidst of FBI that is, technically, part of VASCU Conspiracy, but in reality is seperated from it, being dedicated to more \u2018otherworldly\u2019 matters than most of VASCU dedicated to catching serial killers. The so called \u201cX-Files\u201d are denomination on the cases normal FBI do not have rational resolution. Write up is based on the time of series first season.<br /> <br /> <b><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Fox \u201cSpooky\u201d Mulder</span></i></b><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Believer<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Naive<br /> <b>Profession:</b> Detective ( FBI Agent)<br /> <b>Organization:</b> Vanguard Serial Crimes Unit ( Cell called \u2018X-Files\u2019 )<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 4, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 3, Investigation 4 (Crimes Scens), Medicine 1, Politics 2, Occult 4 (UFO, Conspiracy Theories), Science 1<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 2 (Running), Brawl 2, Drive 1, Firearms 3 (Pistols), Stealth 2, Survival 1, Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Empathy 3 (Motives), Intimidation 1, Socialize 1, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Eye for the Strange, Danger Sense, Indomitable, Investigative Aide (Occult), Library 1 (Occult \u2013 Basement Office in FBI HQ ), Professional Training 3 ( Detective; Empathy, Investigation &amp; Occult ), Tolerance for Biology, Trained Observer 3, Contacts ( FBI Agents, Science Experts, Conspiracy Theorists, Government Informants )<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 6 ( He <i>is</i> a bit Spooky )<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 6<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 11<br /> <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Obsession ( Samantha, Often )<br /> <b>Aspirations: </b>Find Samantha, Uncover Government Conspiracy<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i>Dana Scully</i></b></span><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Rational<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Doubting<br /> <b>Profession:</b> Doctor ( FBI Agent)<br /> <b>Organization:</b> Vanguard Serial Crimes Unit ( Cell called \u2018X-Files\u2019 )<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 4<br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 3, Investigation 3 (Crime Scenes), Medicine 3 (Autopsies), Politics 1, Science 3<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 2, Drive 1, Firearms 3 (Pistols), Stealth 2, Survival 1, Weaponry 2<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Empathy 2 (Motives, Mental Health), Persausion 2, Intimidation 1, Socialize 2, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Common Sense, Danger Sense, Indomitable, Patient, Professional Training 3 ( Doctor; Empathy, Investigation &amp; Medicine ), Tolerance for Biology, Trained Observer 1, Small-Framed, Contacts ( FBI Agents, Science Experts, Medical Community )<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 8 ( She <i>is</i> a bit hard standing )<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 4<br /> <b>Health:</b> 6<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Spooked ( Often )<br /> <b>Aspirations: </b>Helping Mulder be objective, Write rational rapports","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-03-2016, 06:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}